From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Scattering fog

Fog { fogType "SCATTERING" }: a single-scattering medium in HDR
(density, colour, Henyey-Greenstein anisotropy, box), drawn as a post
pass before bloom and tone mapping, and by robot Camera devices (colour)
too. It is lit by the directional lights through the baked light
occlusion layers and by the sky it scatters along each view direction
(Fog.ambientRadiance: the sky against its phase, 9 x 8 directions),
capped in front of geometry by what that table gives. Near the viewer
it reads the sun's shadow maps in steps that grow with distance
(shafts), the second sun shaded like the first.

Bounds: a zero boxSize axis leaves the medium unbounded along it;
Fog.boxFalloff thins density outside the box, exponentially, and
Fog.boxFalloffHorizontal over that distance past its sides. Far haze
converges to Fog.horizonRadiance (the sky just above the horizon, by
azimuth); over the part of a ray outside the box's footprint, surfaces
take that colour by 1 - e^(-length / Fog.hazeDistance). Past the 400 m
marched with sun occlusion, a few unoccluded steps carry the haze to
the horizon. Depth is decoded as 1 - near/d (zero-to-one clip depth),
and the light layers are found without indexing their heights by a
variable.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0008-scattering-fog: 1-2 ms
- 0014-fog-layer
- 0018-fog-horizon
- 0020-horizon-haze
- 0021-fog-falloff-outside
- 0028-fog-light-occlusion: the fog's added light vs Cycles x1.34 vs
  x1.34
- 0029-fog-depth: brightness vs Cycles 0.79-1.20x -> 0.96-1.23x
- 0031-fog-shafts
- 0032-backlit-foliage (its fog part)
- 0033-fog-sky-phase: overview brightness vs Cycles 1.66x -> 1.14x;
  backlit shadows (p10) 3.1x -> 1.55x
- 0034-fog-box-sides: region canopy from 60 m vs Cycles 2.4x -> 1.6x
- 0035-camera-fog: drone camera frames show the forest's haze
- 0045-fog-layer-search: fog pass 7.4-10.3 -> 6.9-8.9 ms at 1920x1080
- 0068-distance-haze
